Project Submission and Assessment
The project submission process is similar to what you used in Project 9. Here’s the workflow:

Submission Workflow
Make a pull request from your stage 1 branch into main.
Copy the link and submit it on the project submission page.
Your project will be reviewed within 24 hours using the assessment criteria below.
Make your fixes and push the changes to the same branch.
This process continues until the project is accepted.
After it is accepted, you should merge the Stage 1 branch into main.
💡 If you need a refresher on this topic, refer back to our chapter on Git branches.

Assessment criteria
The final project review is different from the other code reviews you have experienced so far. The criteria our instructors use are more demanding — but also allow for acceptance without all criteria being met: each point in the checklist is given a point value, and you need to get 80 points out of 100 to pass the stage.

